# ==================================================================================
# .FILE
#   .bash_logout
#
# .SYNOPSIS
#   Login shell termination script.
#
# .DESCRIPTION
#   This script is executed automatically when a Bash login shell exits. It is
#   commonly used to perform session cleanup tasks such as clearing the terminal,
#   removing temporary files, stopping background processes, or executing other
#   logout routines before the session ends.
#
# .PARAMETER
#   N/A
#   This file does not accept parameters; it is sourced automatically by Bash
#   during login shell termination.
#
# .INPUTS
#   None
#
# .OUTPUTS
#   Session cleanup actions and logout-related tasks.
#
# .NOTES
#   Version       : 1.0
#   Author        : @ZouariOmar (zouariomar20@gmail.com)
#   Created       : 2026-07-29
#   Change Log    : Initial documentation
#
# .EXAMPLE
#   N/A — this file is sourced automatically by Bash when a login shell exits.
# ==================================================================================

#
# none
#
